## WHAT THE WORK IS
**General property (binding):** *the purchase result gains ONE member, `PurchaseResult.Projection` (`RecurringProjection?`, the rental type reused, with its own `[JsonIgnore(Condition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull)]`, not `required`, last in the record), formed only from figures the result already holds, reading them and writing none; every pre-existing member of every input and result is byte-equal to base under all three serializers below; a priced quote with no recurring source (Q-2, Q-3) is byte-equal to base as a whole; no input member, no issue, no sentence a person could read is added.* Member and local names are English technical; no screen word.

**The six measures, purchase reading (binding unless Tuesday overrides Q-2 to Q-5 at the stamp).** Sources: **S1** each section whose `ClickResult.Supplies` is set (section rates with a supplies model; its figures are PER DEVICE and scale by that supplies model's `DeviceQuantity`, `Supplies.DeviceQuantity`, exactly as X-18's `SuppliesProfit` does, never by the section's `DeviceQuantity` or fleet quantity); **S2** the deal usage when `Usage.Supplies` is set (WHOLE DEAL, never multiplied again); **S3** a stated fee (X-38: `PurchaseResult.MonthlyManagedServiceCost` not null). Let k be `Supplies.DeviceQuantity` for S1 and 1 for S2.
| measure | Monthly (sum over S1 and S2, plus S3 where named) | Contract (Q-4: the result's own contract figures) |
|---|---|---|
| Pages | k x (`MonthlyMonoPages` + `MonthlyColourPages`) | k x `ContractPages` |
| Click cost | k x (`MonthlyMonoPages` x `MonoCpp` + `MonthlyColourPages` x `ColourCpp`) (the CPPs on the same `ClickResult` / `DealUsageResult`) | k x `ContractSuppliesCost` |
| Managed-service cost | S3 `MonthlyManagedServiceCost`, else 0 | `ContractManagedServiceCost`, else 0 |
| Click revenue | k x (`MonthlyMonoPages` x applied mono + `MonthlyColourPages` x applied colour) (`AppliedMonoClick`/`AppliedColourClick`; the deal's `?? 0` as X-26; NEVER an X-30 target) | k x `ContractClickRevenue` |
| Service revenue | S3 `MonthlyManagedServiceSell`, else 0 | `ContractManagedServiceSell`, else 0 |
| Recurring GP | click revenue - click cost + service revenue - managed-service cost (Q-5: no shortfall) | `SuppliesProfit` + (`ContractManagedServiceSell` - `ContractManagedServiceCost`, when stated) = `DealProfit` - `HardwareProfit` (Q-4: includes the X-17/X-27 replacement shortfall) |
Annual = Monthly x `WorkbookRules.MonthsPerYear`, exactly, for every measure (no rounding step anywhere). **Presence (Q-2):** `Projection` is set iff the quote is priced AND at least one source exists; otherwise null (omitted). **Q-3:** a section rate or a deal usage WITHOUT a supplies model is not a source (the result holds no cost for it; projecting its revenue would show a profit with no cost), and its pages are not counted. Measure first and list in STATUS DESIGN every site that forms `SuppliesProfit`, `DealProfit`, `ContractSuppliesCost`, `ContractClickRevenue`, `ContractPages` and their readers (`git grep -n` with a control), and for each say: read by the projection / not / why.
